reagent-name-dh-omnireazin = omnireazine
reagent-desc-dh-omnireazin = The Association's universal medicine, standard since MB-2M. Stops bleeding, knits light and moderate wounds and dulls pain. It does not treat heavy wounds or restore limbs. The soldier it helped is still wounded. They can just keep fighting. For now.

dh-entity-effect-guidebook-omnireazin =
    { $chance ->
        [1] Knits
        *[other] knit
    } light and moderate wounds (up to {$amount} at a time) without touching heavy wounds or fractures; the pain returns once it wears off

dh-omnireazin-wears-off = The omnireazine lets go. The pain comes back.
dh-omnireazin-phantom-start = Something aches where nothing should hurt any more. It doesn't go away.
dh-omnireazin-phantom-1 = Old wounds ache, though they closed long ago.
dh-omnireazin-phantom-2 = It feels like shrapnel tearing through your arm again.
dh-omnireazin-phantom-3 = The pain comes from nowhere, and nothing takes it away.
dh-omnireazin-phantom-4 = It burns under your ribs, just like that time.
dh-omnireazin-depersonalization-1 = You look at your hands. They are someone else's.
dh-omnireazin-depersonalization-2 = Your body moves on its own. You watch it from the outside.
dh-omnireazin-depersonalization-3 = This isn't your body. They just issued it to you with the armour.
dh-omnireazin-depersonalization-4 = You can't tell where you end and the drug begins.
dh-omnireazin-depersonalization-5 = Your fingers move a beat late, as if someone else is steering them.
